      "review": [
        {
          "paragraph": 31,
          "reasons": [
            "Reference to visual material"
          ],
          "text": "The atomic-requirement record and the corpus entry that wrap this predicate — requirement_id, scope_tags, standard_version, source_hash, predicate_hash, status — are shown in Figure 1."
        },
        {
          "paragraph": 55,
          "reasons": [
            "Reference to visual material"
          ],
          "text": "The verifier result binds that design to a released predicate. The certificate then records the design hash, predicate hashes, standard versions, the assumption ledger, the world-model reference, the witness bundle, the verifier policy, and the per-layer results. The assumption ledger is a frozen record of the inputs, exclusions, and conservative choices the design was made under. Figure 3 makes the binding explicit."
        }
      ],
      "file": "en/executable-standards.txt"
